The test vehicle travels at target speed V1 on a straight road. A target vehicle traveling at speed V2 along the centerline of the adjacent lane is positioned ahead. V1 > V2. The target vehicle maintains a constant speed and changes lanes toward the current lane of the test vehicle at a cycle time t. After completing the lane change, the target vehicle continues traveling along the centerline of its current lane. The time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the target vehicle to reach the collision point.